scripts/rebase-push.md:17:`--continue --no-push` requires `--keep-on-conflict` (rejected at parse time with exit 3 otherwise) so a nested conflict during the local-only resolution loop never silently aborts the in-progress rebase. Every legitimate caller of `--continue --no-push` (the early_rebase Phase 4 invocation in `skills/implement/references/conflict-resolution.md`) already passes `--keep-on-conflict`; the rejection is defense-in-depth for any future caller.
