skills/research/scripts/validate-citations.md:195:| `__VC_SETSID_DONE` | internal marker for the Linux `setsid` re-exec — set just before `exec setsid` so the re-exec'd child inherits it (idempotency guard preventing infinite recursion) AND the budget-exhaustion handler reads it as the "running in dedicated session" gate that authorizes `kill -- -$$` on Linux |
scripts/check-stale-plugin.sh:2:# check-stale-plugin.sh — Detect version skew between the installed larch plugin
