scripts/test-tracking-issue-read-sentinel.md:48:The harness is Makefile-only (not referenced from any `SKILL.md`), so agent-lint would flag it as dead. An exclusion entry in `agent-lint.toml` sits next to the existing `scripts/test-tracking-issue-write.sh` exclusion, with the same rationale.
scripts/implement-fork-env.md:32:Step 0's atomic three-call setup (`create-branch.sh --check` → `session-entry-gate.sh` → `session-setup.sh`) creates `SESSION_TMPDIR` only inside the third call. The fork bootstrap must run BEFORE that sequence so `--caller-env` can be passed through to `session-setup.sh`. There is no `IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR` yet. Forcing the orchestrator to allocate a bootstrap tmpdir before the fork-env helper would expand the pre-Step-0 surface unnecessarily; the helper owns its own bootstrap.
scripts/cleanup-tmpdir.md:1:# scripts/cleanup-tmpdir.sh — contract
scripts/cleanup-tmpdir.md:3:`scripts/cleanup-tmpdir.sh` is the guarded `rm -rf` invoked by every skill's terminal cleanup step (`/implement` Step 18, `/design` Step 5b, `/review` cleanup, `/research` cleanup, `/fix-issue` Step 8, `/issue` cleanup). The script validates that `--dir` is non-empty and resolves under `/tmp/`, `/private/tmp/`, `/var/folders/` (macOS), or `${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/larch/sessions/` before removing — this is the load-bearing guard against accidentally deleting a non-tmp directory if a caller passes the wrong variable. Exit 0 on successful removal (or absent dir); exit 1 on validation failure or argument error. Caller-side guards (e.g. `/implement` Step 18's basename + session-id sanity check) decide WHEN to invoke; this script decides WHETHER the path is safe to remove.
scripts/cleanup-tmpdir.md:7:Regression coverage lives in `scripts/test-cleanup-tmpdir.sh` (sibling contract: `scripts/test-cleanup-tmpdir.md`) and `scripts/test-cache-root-validation.sh`, wired through `make test-cleanup-tmpdir` and `make test-cache-root-validation`.
