skills/implement/references/rebase-rebump-subprocedure.md:34:   The helper walks back from `HEAD` and removes the most recent matching bump commit within its search depth, so `HEAD=larch-log-flush`, `HEAD~1=bump` is an expected success shape.
skills/implement/references/rebase-rebump-subprocedure.md:41:   **step10 / step12 family**: after dropping the bump commit, re-write the token/timing batches with updated data, then commit the flush (unless `no_logs_commit=true`). Running this BEFORE the rebase (step 2) serves two purposes: (1) it cleans up any uncommitted larch-log writes from Steps 9a.1/11 that would otherwise cause `rebase-push.sh --no-push` to fail on a dirty working tree; (2) it keeps log-maintenance commits out of the post-rebase / post-re-bump replay window, which reduces avoidable conflicts and preserves a cleaner retry shape. This ordering is hygiene, not a hard prerequisite for `drop-bump-commit.sh` now that it can walk back below `HEAD`. `larch-log.sh commit` does not push; step 5 performs the push. When `no_logs_commit=true`, the writes still run (to preserve the tmpdir artifacts) but the commit step is skipped; no dirty-tree issue arises because prior commit calls were also skipped.
skills/implement/references/rebase-rebump-subprocedure.md:49:   "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/larch-log.sh" write --log-root "$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/larch-logs" --skill implement --run-id "$RUN_ID" --batch token-report --input-file "$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/token-report-rendered.json" || true
skills/implement/references/rebase-rebump-subprocedure.md:50:   "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/larch-log.sh" write --log-root "$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/larch-logs" --skill implement --run-id "$RUN_ID" --batch timing-report --input-file "$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/timing-report-rendered.json" || true
skills/implement/references/rebase-rebump-subprocedure.md:52:     "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/larch-log.sh" commit --log-root "$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/larch-logs" --skill implement --run-id "$RUN_ID" || true
skills/implement/references/rebase-rebump-subprocedure.md:143:   **Critical (step12 family only)**: Do NOT simply "log and return to caller" on push failure. That would let the merge loop proceed to `ACTION=merge` on a remote branch that does NOT contain the fresh bump commit, violating the feature's core invariant. `merge-pr.sh` reads local git state for its HEAD-OID precondition, branch-range bump-subject scan, `origin/main` refresh, and origin `plugin.json` same-version gate, while `ci-wait.sh` and the final `gh pr merge` operation still act on the remote PR / branch state. Unpushed local commits remain invisible to the merge itself.
skills/implement/references/rebase-rebump-subprocedure.md:147:   Umbrella #348 Phase 5 retargets this step from the PR body to the committed `version-bump-reasoning` batch under `larch-logs/implement/$RUN_ID/` (see `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/implement/references/summary-comment-template.md` for the summary-comment contract). Unlike the old PR-body refresh, this step is a no-op when no run id is resolved for the session.
