scripts/write-session-id.md:1:# scripts/write-session-id.sh — contract
scripts/write-session-id.md:3:`scripts/write-session-id.sh` is the single-call wrapper around the `uuidgen`-or-fallback session-id snippet that `/implement` Step 0 emits to `$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/session-id`. The id pins design-manifest freshness: `read-design-manifest.sh` rejects a manifest whose stored `SESSION_ID` does not match the value in this file.
scripts/write-session-id.md:11:- If `PATH` already exists and is non-empty, exit 0 without modifying it. This keeps the wrapper idempotent now that `session-setup.sh` creates `session-id` directly.
scripts/write-session-id.md:12:- If `uuidgen` is on `PATH`, write `uuidgen` output to `PATH`.
scripts/write-session-id.md:13:- Otherwise fall back to `$(basename $(dirname PATH))` — the session tmpdir basename, which is unique per run and adequate as a freshness key when uuidgen is absent.
scripts/write-session-id.md:21:No sibling regression harness — the wrapper is two lines of shell behind a uuidgen-vs-fallback predicate. Manual smoke verification at write-time covers both paths; CI's shellcheck pass covers syntax regressions.
scripts/cleanup-tmpdir.md:3:`scripts/cleanup-tmpdir.sh` is the guarded `rm -rf` invoked by every skill's terminal cleanup step (`/implement` Step 18, `/design` Step 5b, `/review` cleanup, `/research` cleanup, `/fix-issue` Step 8, `/issue` cleanup). The script validates that `--dir` is non-empty and resolves under `/tmp/`, `/private/tmp/`, `/var/folders/` (macOS), or `${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/larch/sessions/` before removing — this is the load-bearing guard against accidentally deleting a non-tmp directory if a caller passes the wrong variable. Exit 0 on successful removal (or absent dir); exit 1 on validation failure or argument error. Caller-side guards (e.g. `/implement` Step 18's basename + session-id sanity check) decide WHEN to invoke; this script decides WHETHER the path is safe to remove.
