scripts/test-hook-block-skill-relevant-checks.md:5:The harness constructs disposable `.larch-keepalive` fixtures under `${XDG_CACHE_HOME}/larch/sessions`, then asserts that both `tool_input.skill` and `tool_input.skill_name` shapes deny `/relevant-checks` inside active `claude-implement-*` and `claude-review-*` sessions. It also covers `larch:relevant-checks`, non-target skills, cwd mismatch (allow), hook-session-id mismatch (deny — confirms resolver binds on cwd + TTL only, never on the hook payload's `session_id`), stale keepalive TTL (allow), and missing-`jq` fail-open behavior. A `/tmp`-fallback fixture exercises the resolver's acceptance of `/tmp/claude-implement-*` direct children.
