scripts/hook-block-skill-relevant-checks.md:7:Input: Claude Code hook JSON on stdin. The hook reads `tool_name`, `tool_input.skill`, `tool_input.skill_name`, and `cwd`. The hook payload's `.session_id` (Claude transcript namespace) is intentionally NOT consulted — `session-setup.sh` generates the keepalive's `SESSION_ID` independently via `uuidgen`, and the two namespaces never match in production. The resolver binds on `cwd` + keepalive TTL only; see `scripts/lib-resolve-active-larch-session.md` for details. Both `relevant-checks` and `larch:relevant-checks` are blocked; all other skills are allowed.
