I would keep this as a narrow `/design` completion extension, not a redesign of the run-log system. Add `planned -> [PLANNED] ` to [scripts/tracking-issue-write.sh](<OPERATOR_REPO_PATH>/scripts/tracking-issue-write.sh) and teach [scripts/lib-title-markers.sh](<OPERATOR_REPO_PATH>/scripts/lib-title-markers.sh) to treat `[PLANNED]` as a managed lifecycle prefix. In [skills/design/SKILL.md](<OPERATOR_REPO_PATH>/skills/design/SKILL.md), Step 5 should remain the single completion boundary: after `plan-block-write.sh` succeeds, run `tracking-issue-write.sh rename --state planned`, then flush design logs, create/merge the log PR, and only then call `cleanup-tmpdir.sh`. Title rename should be best-effort but visible, consistent with existing terminal rename behavior.

For logs and PR flow, I would avoid changing `scripts/larch-log.sh commit` unless absolutely necessary because it is shared by `/implement` and `/review`, and its commit-message behavior is a broad contract. The smallest safer shape is a design-specific helper, probably under `skills/design/scripts/` or `scripts/`, that copies all non-symlink files from `$DESIGN_TMPDIR` into `larch-logs/design/<run-id>/` with the same tmpdir/secrets redaction pipeline, commits only that directory with `chore(larch-logs): flush design run <run-id> [skip ci]`, creates a minimal PR with `scripts/create-pr.sh`, merges it with `gh pr merge --squash --admin --delete-branch`, and then runs local cleanup for the branch. Use the existing `--run-id` if supplied, otherwise `$DESIGN_TMPDIR/session-id`.

Main regressions to guard against: accidentally triggering this during nested `/implement` design, leaking raw temp paths or secrets in committed logs, deleting a branch the user already had before `/design`, and breaking existing lifecycle title stripping. I would mitigate with explicit tests for `planned` in `scripts/test-tracking-issue-write.sh`, a new offline helper harness with stubbed `git`/`gh` proving order and path scoping, and a SKILL-level assertion that Step 5 orders `plan-block-write` before log flush/PR and cleanup after. Because committing full `$DESIGN_TMPDIR` expands the outbound publication surface, update `SECURITY.md` and `docs/run-logs.md` with the redaction and retention contract. No files modified.
